handshakes and congratulations as  britain and india announced new deals on  defence and green energy as well as  plans to fast-track a free trade  agreement  between prime minister boris johnson  saying he and indian counterpart  narendra modi have committed to trade an  investment worth 14 billion dollars  which will create 11 000 jobs in the uk  a decades-long commitment that will not  only  forge tighter bonds between us but  support your goal and the renderer of  make in india  he's the latest western leader in new  delhi to try to entice india away from  its reliance on moscow by promising to  step up cooperation  johnson said britain would help india  build its own fighter jets and they'd  agreed to work together to meet military  threats from land sea air space and  cyber attacks too  russia is india's biggest military  supplier and indian leaders have refused  to condemn moscow for invading ukraine  while the kremlin faces crippling  sanctions india has increased oil  imports from russia  analyst suggests india is focused closer  to home china has been waging border  aggression against india  and no western leader  has condemned the chinese border  aggression  so india is not willing to take sides in  a conflict in which  india has  no stakes directly modi did though push  for an end to the war  we emphasize the need for an immediate  ceasefire in ukraine and the use of  dialogue and diplomacy for resolving  issues  johnson says he doesn't expect india to  change its position on russia but said  modi has tried to use his influence on  president putin france he's intervened  several times with  with vladimir putin really to ask him  what you know what on earth he thinks  he's doing  and where he thinks this is going  while johnson is walking away from his  india trip with promises of a lucrative  free trade deal his visit didn't go  without a hitch there's been outrage in  some quarters after this photo  opportunity at the british construction  equipment firm jcb owned by a  conservative party donor  just days after jcb bulldozers were seen  flattening properties in a largely  muslim neighborhood  rights groups say the demolitions are  part of a pattern of religious  polarization by modi's hindu nationalist  bjp  amnesty international criticized  johnson's photo op as ignorant saying  that his silence on the incident was  deafening alexi o'brien al jazeera
 

